// biz.rut — THE BIZ PACKAGE (the two-package law): the todolist's
// domain and app — the sources, the derived counts line, the machine
// as MUTATIONS, the two view builders, and the app shell. ONE module,
// SEVERAL files (RFC 0041 §5, the multi-lib entry: this base +
// `entry.libs`, spliced in manifest order — a name in any file is
// module-visible in every file, so the sections stay one namespace).
//
// THE FILE MAP (rut.toml's `entry.libs` — the array IS the order):
//   ./domain.rut   the domain types + the machine's pure scans
//   ./world.rut    THE WORLD: the handles bundle + world_boot
//   ./entries.rut  the DOM-free host-test surface + the probe fixtures
//   ./app.rut      the shell (AppRoot, dispatch, paint) + the views
//
// Everything here speaks the store's two-verb surface and nothing
// else of it:
//
//   reads    store.get(atom)            (sources and deriveds alike)
//   writes   store.set(source, v)       (plain)
//            store.set(mutation, arg)   (the machine's verbs)
//
// THERE IS NO domain container. The store is a DECOUPLED-BIZ design (the ui
// package's Store knows no todo); what biz owns is HANDLES — the
// sources, the derived, the mutations — bundled in `World`, the state
// record the host re-passes every turn. The machine's counters
// (next_todo/next_req) are sources too: state lives in the store, and
// without a domain container there is nowhere else for state to live
// (the old "what is not an atom" list shrinks to nothing).
//
// THE MACHINE AS MUTATIONS (the survey §1.3 mutation-atom rejection is
// overturned — its recorded reason predates first-class fns): every
// multi-step write is a mutation fn whose ctx exposes get + set; all
// writes land in the ONE write lane inside the store. The answers stay
// DATA ((line, err) — the entry-err shape); the timers stay OUT (the
// mutations never touch the clock — the app books tim_after from the
// returned Req). view NEVER writes (the survey §4.2 law, kept).
//
// THE TURN SHAPE (kept): one on_event entry, one paint per turn, the
// ONE keyed-diff render. The FLUSH IS GONE (pull-on-read): paint does
// no flush — the view's first get computes what this turn's writes
// staled, at most once per write-set. The status line reads
// store.get(counts$) — byte-identical to every phase before.
//
// THE LAW GATE (tests/app_law.rs pins the import set): the store's
// vocabulary, the widget vocabulary, the framework's names, and ONE
// crossing name, tim_after. No tag, no token, no listener id, no
// machinery trait (Readable/Writable are ui-private — biz cannot name
// them even to import them).

use ui::{
    Store, Source, Derived, Mutation,
    Widget, T1Root, t1_mount, t1_render, t1_subject,
    col, row, card, field, check, text, done, pending, muted, btn, quiet,
};
use pouch::{ Vec };
use nmapset::{ HashMap };
use web::{ tim_after };

